␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-d  --minimal  Try hard to find a smaller set of changes.␀ç∂␀␀␀␀--horizon-lines=NUM  Keep NUM lines of the common prefix and suffix.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-S FILE  --starting-file=FILE  Start with FILE when comparing directories.
␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-X FILE  --exclude-from=FILE  Exclude files that match any pattern in FILE.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-x PAT  --exclude=PAT  Exclude files that match PAT.␀çt&␀çº'␀␀␀␀-s  --report-identical-files  Report when two files are the same.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-P  --unidirectional-new-file  Treat absent first files as empty.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-N  --new-file  Treat absent files as empty.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-r  --recursive  Recursively compare any subdirectories found.␀ê-T  --initial-tab  Make tabs line up by prepending a tab.
␀êçt&␀-t  --expand-tabs  Expand tabs to spaces in output.␀ç∂␀␀␀␀çø␀␀␀␀-l  --paginate  Pass the output through `pr' to paginate it.␀çv␀    %c'\OOO'  the character with octal code OOO
␀Îêêêêêêêêêêêêê    %c'C'  the single character C␀    %%  %␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê  Either GFMT or LFMT may contain:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê    %[-][WIDTH][.[PREC]]{doxX}n  printf-style spec for input line number␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê    %l  contents of line, excluding any trailing newline␀    %L  contents of line␀  LFMT may contain:␀        M  L+1␀        E  F-1␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê        N  number of lines = L-F+1␀        L  last line number␀        F  first line number␀çt&␀      LETTERs are as follows for new group, lower case for old group:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê    %[-][WIDTH][.[PREC]]{doxX}LETTER  printf-style spec for LETTER␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê    %=  lines common to FILE1 and FILE2␀    %>  lines from FILE2␀    %<  lines from FILE1␀  GFMT may contain:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê  LTYPE is `old', `new', or `unchanged'.  GTYPE is LTYPE or `changed'.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê--LTYPE-line-format=LFMT  Similar, but format LTYPE input lines with LFMT.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê--line-format=LFMT  Similar, but format all input lines with LFMT.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê--GTYPE-group-format=GFMT  Similar, but format GTYPE input groups with GFMT.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-DNAME  --ifdef=NAME  Output merged file to show `#ifdef NAME' diffs.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê  --suppress-common-lines  Do not output common lines.␀âˆçº'␀␀␀␀  --left-column  Output only the left column of common lines.␀âˆ  -w NUM  --width=NUM  Output at most NUM (default 130) characters per line.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-y  --side-by-side  Output in two columns.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-n  --rcs  Output an RCS format diff.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-e  --ed  Output an ed script.␀ê-q  --brief  Output only whether files differ.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê  -F RE  --show-function-line=RE  Show the most recent line matching RE.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê  -p  --show-c-function  Show which C function each change is in.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê  -L LABEL  --label LABEL  Use LABEL instead of file name.␀êçt&␀  -NUM  Use NUM context lines.␀ê-u  -U NUM  --unified[=NUM]  Output NUM (default 2) lines of unified context.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-c  -C NUM  --context[=NUM]  Output NUM (default 2) lines of copied context.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-a  --text  Treat all files as text.
␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê--binary  Read and write data in binary mode.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-I RE  --ignore-matching-lines=RE  Ignore changes whose lines all match RE.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-B  --ignore-blank-lines  Ignore changes whose lines are all blank.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-b  --ignore-space-change  Ignore changes in the amount of white space.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-w  --ignore-all-space  Ignore all white space.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêê-i  --ignore-case  Consider upper- and lower-case to be the same.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêUsage: %s [OPTION]... FILE1 FILE2

